---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="BalEval Benchmark | DoAI × ILPRL Project"
  description="A unified multimodal foundation benchmark and baseline suite for Nepali NLP and LLM evaluation."
  activeTab="projects"
>
  <div class="detail-header">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span>/</span> <a href="/projects">Projects</a> <span>/</span> <span>BalEval</span>
      </div>
      <div class="project-badges" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
        <span class="badge badge-progress">In Progress</span>
        <span class="badge badge-category">Evaluation & Benchmarks</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="detail-title">BalEval: Multimodal Nepali Foundation Benchmark</h1>
      <p class="detail-subtitle">
        A Unified Empirical Evaluation Suite Pairing Natively Multimodal Retrieval with Generative Foundation Reasoning for Nepali.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="container">
    <div class="detail-grid">
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="detail-main">
        <div class="detail-section">
          <h2>1. Charter & Research Scope</h2>
          <p>
            The primary objective of <strong>BalEval</strong> is to execute a rigorous, publication-grade empirical milestone for the Nepali language: consolidating 22 years of fragmented legacy NLP tools into a unified foundation benchmark and fine-tuned baseline suite.
          </p>
          <p>
            BalEval pairs <strong>EmbeddingGemma 2 (740M)</strong> for natively multimodal retrieval with <strong>Gemma 4 E4B (4.2B)</strong> for generative reasoning across Devanagari text, scanned historical archives, and speech transcripts.
          </p>
          <div class="callout">
            <strong>Core Objective:</strong> Replace disjoint pipelines with a single open foundation benchmark (AST tool evaluation, IFEval verifier, and lexical audit).
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="detail-section">
          <h2>2. 12-Week Sprint Schedule</h2>
          <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.8;">
            <li>
              <strong>Month 1 (Archival Mining & Auditing):</strong> Harvest ILPRL legacy datasets and public sector archives into standardized JSON Lines schema; audit zero-shot baselines.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Month 2 (Multimodal Engineering & Training):</strong> Index scanned citizen charters and audio transcripts into EmbeddingGemma 2 vector store; fine-tune Gemma 4 E4B via 4-bit QLoRA.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Month 3 (Rigorous Evaluation & Capstone Packaging):</strong> Automated AST and IFEval execution, qualitative linguistic review with supervisors, ablation studies, and open-source release (<code>ILPRL/BalEval</code>).
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sidebar -->
      <aside class="detail-sidebar">
        <div class="sidebar-box">
          <h3>Project Metadata</h3>
          <ul class="sidebar-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Candidate / Student</strong>
              Sundeep Dawadi (Dept. of AI, KU)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Academic Supervisor</strong>
              Mr. Sunil Regmi (Lecturer & Coordinator, DoAI)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Mentor & Domain Lead</strong>
              Prof. Dr. Bal Krishna Bal (Dean, SoE & Lead, ILPRL)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Timeline</strong>
              12 Weeks (Weeks 1–12 Sprint)
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Models Evaluated</strong>
              Gemma 4 E4B, EmbeddingGemma 2
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Target Release</strong>
              Hugging Face: <code>ILPRL/BalEval</code>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="sidebar-box">
          <h3>Navigation</h3>
          <a href="/projects" class="btn btn-secondary" style="justify-content: center; width: 100%;">
            ← Back to All Projects
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
